Both traces are now recorded with solid evidence:

**hypre / boomeramg-mpi-cpu** (MPI + OpenMP, no GPU):
- Parallelism: MPI ranks each owning a partition of the ParCSR matrix, OpenMP threading inside kernels
- Communication: mixed point-to-point neighbor halo exchange (`par_csr_pmvcomm.c` Isend/Irecv) for matvec/relaxation at every AMG level, plus scalar reductions for norms
- Latency-sensitive, not bandwidth-sensitive (small neighbor messages, not all-to-all)
- Memory: sparse/irregular kernels → judged memory-bandwidth bound, very low arithmetic intensity, poor cache reuse
- No shared memory windows, no NUMA pinning, no huge pages found
- No parallel I/O library, no checkpoint/restart
- Topology: can run single or multi-node, neighbor placement preferred, no ordered/wavefront dependency

**hypre / boomeramg-mpi-cuda** (MPI + single GPU backend CUDA/HIP/SYCL, mutually exclusive):
- Parallelism: MPI + GPU device kernels for setup (coarsening/interpolation/strength) and solve (relaxation/matvec) phases
- Same neighbor-exchange/reduction communication pattern as CPU, but optionally accelerated by GPU-aware MPI (`--enable-gpu-aware-mpi`) avoiding host staging
- No multi-GPU-per-process coordination found
- Same memory-bandwidth-bound, very-low-arithmetic-intensity judgment carries to device kernels
- Preferred co-location of ranks/GPUs for fast interconnect given latency-sensitive halo exchange

Both traces record only evidence actually found in the source (parcsr_ls, struct_mv, multivector, configure/docs), with proper `absent:` citations for negative claims.
